ROADMAP.md:334:The owner answered these provisionally on 2026-11-05 (A2a; [the decided rows](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core)) and freezes them at A2c. The [Core proposal](legacy/docs/compiler/CORE_PROPOSAL.md) is the background; where it and a decided row differ, the row governs:
ROADMAP.md:405:| R-0559 | Outside-reader pass on the approved Core design, then on each feature ([readers](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-outside-readers)) | Codex, agy and Kimi read the decided rows and the integrated spec through the browsable owner view first; every unclear point and confusion is resolved before the owner's formal read and before the freeze (A2c), while real design questions still go to the owner; Kimi's absence is recorded, not waited on; the check repeats for each feature as it lands ([reading order](docs/decisions.md#outside-readers-ordering), owner, 2026-11-07); Home: tooling (the owner view) and the recorded reads. Gate: each participating reader's read recorded, Kimi's recorded absence accepted in its place when it is unavailable, and every confusion resolved before the freeze ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | R-0555, R-0571, R-0496, R-0560, R-0574 |
ROADMAP.md:406:| R-0511 | Representative design proofs before Core freezes, then cumulative slices with honest theorem scopes | the four A2b theorems are kernel-checked against the proposed `Spec.lean`, without `native_decide`, with their full obligations (decision row Q9.14): `reset_fresh` (a reset gives a brand distinct from every live brand, resets in a loop give pairwise-distinct brands, and the new allocator's operations refuse values of an old brand); `defer_cleanup_releases` (every structured exit runs the deferred calls in reverse registration order, releases each held loan after its call, and preserves the allocator-dependency check); `open_mut_freezes_root` (a mutable heap open excludes every other access to its root, and a shared open never grants a write); `rep_roundtrip` (encode then decode is the identity for `u8` to `u64`, `bool` and the empty struct); each later slice states its theorem scope (A2a was approved 2026-11-05) | — |
ROADMAP.md:407:| R-0567 | Core freeze (A2c) | the owner approves the freeze of the integrated scopes after A2i's complete acceptance (the four A2b theorems, the integration proofs, the semantic contract, the modular layout, the browsable owner view and the outside-reader pass); the frozen scope is the foundation C1–C10, accepted after its Lean implementation, kernel proofs, interaction tests, review by the four models and the owner ([question 1](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q1)); afterwards a change to a frozen foundation definition is an owner decision, re-runs the earlier proofs and is recorded in `docs/decisions.md`; PROPOSED is removed from its header in the freeze change | R-0571, R-0574, R-0496, R-0560, R-0555, R-0559, R-0607, R-0608, R-0609, R-0610, R-0611, R-0612, R-0613, R-0614, R-0615, R-0616 |
ROADMAP.md:410:| R-0571 | Integrate the proposed spec before the freeze (A2i): shared Core interfaces, one integrated semantics and interaction proofs (decided 2026-11-06) | the parts share Core interfaces and one semantics; kernel-checked proofs cover a borrow across deferred cleanup, an allocator reset with outstanding loans and cleanup that needs authority; README obligations [O7 and O9](ConcreteSpec/README.md) are discharged; no `sorry`, no `native_decide`, only the three standard axioms | R-0511, R-0560, R-0607, R-0608, R-0609, R-0610, R-0611, R-0612, R-0613, R-0614, R-0615, R-0616 |
ROADMAP.md:411:| R-0588 | Fact and capability preservation across indirect calls, specialization and packages | at A2i, the integrated spec states that capability, allocation, termination, may-abort and evidence facts are preserved through indirect calls, monomorphization and package boundaries; at A3, the theorem is stated with its holes; at B0 and B1, it is proved for each slice's fragment and the facts query reports through these boundaries; later fragments prove it as they land | R-0571 |
ROADMAP.md:412:| R-0592 | Fix the checker result type, the leakage-trace interface and the byte-accounting instrumentation before the freeze ([diagnostics](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-diagnostics-2026-11-06), [memory](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-memory-2026-11-06), [information flow](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06), 2026-11-06) | the integrated spec's checker returns a typed result with one refusal constructor per premise; the semantics carries the leakage-trace interface (branches, addresses, allocation sizes, loop counts, variable-time operands) and sized-allocation accounting per allocator lineage; each is kernel-checked against its examples; changing them after the freeze would be a Core change | R-0571 |
ROADMAP.md:413:| R-0602 | An extensible observable-event kind in Core | before the freeze, Core has an observable-event kind that later events extend; secret wipes are protected as observable; device semantics come later | R-0571 |
ROADMAP.md:414:| R-0603 | Rule revisions, the retired-ID registry and `spec_version` | each Lean rule has its own revision, bumped when its meaning changes, including through dependencies, and checked; retired rule IDs stay in a registry; every output carries one `spec_version` header covering every record (0.x before the freeze, 1.0 at A2c, bumped by every normative change), checked in CI and distinct from the product version | R-0571 |
ROADMAP.md:415:| R-0607 | Foundation C1: execution, calls and cleanup ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c1-execution-calls-and-cleanup), [decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-foundation)) | machine configurations, the labeled single-step relation and its results (completion, return, labeled break and continue, abort) are in Lean; left-to-right evaluation, call by typed identity, and cleanup on every structured exit (inner scope first, reverse registration order, abort runs none) are rules with accepted and refused examples; sequencing, scope restoration and cleanup preservation are kernel-checked, and the old `Cleanup` fragment is ported and deleted; Home: spec (`Syntax`, `Semantics`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate and the proof-integrity jobs over its theorems | R-0610, R-0612 |
ROADMAP.md:416:| R-0608 | Foundation C2: scalars, failure and arithmetic ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c2-scalars-failure-and-arithmetic)) | the mathematical scalar values, their bit representations, every operation's contract and the error classification are in Lean, with the correspondence laws; traps, unsafe stuckness, allocation failure and fuel exhaustion stay separate outcomes (Q6.7); the trap kinds' names wait for the owner before the first slice that prints them ([question 9](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q9)); Home: spec (`Types`, `Scalar`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate (each operation's accepted and failing examples) and the proof-integrity jobs | — |
ROADMAP.md:417:| R-0609 | Foundation C3: target, layout and representation ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c3-target-layout-and-representation)) | the read-only target profile (address width, pointer storage, length width, byte order, address spaces, maximum object sizes) and the layout interface are in Lean, with the existing 64-bit little-endian profile as an instance ([question 3](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q3)); the layout laws (alignment, size, in-bounds non-overlapping fields, unique discriminants, valid tag decoding) are proved for the native, C and packed algorithms; `i32` enum tags, no niches, `Secret<T>` with `T`'s layout; `rep_roundtrip` is restated over it and `Rep` is deleted; Home: spec (`Target`, `Layout`, `Values`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate and the proof-integrity jobs | R-0608 |
ROADMAP.md:418:| R-0610 | Foundation C4: byte memory and value validity ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c4-byte-memory-and-value-validity)) | the hybrid state (structured places, byte and provenance blocks, the partial projection and `Rep`, materialization on raw address-taking, `expose` or foreign use) is in Lean ([question 2](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q2)), with the typed-write store rule, partial decoding, access validity, provenance and `from_exposed` (Q3.9), zero-size slots and the allocator availability laws (Q1.11); round-trip and decode-validity are kernel-checked; Home: spec (`Store`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate and the proof-integrity jobs | R-0609 |
ROADMAP.md:419:| R-0611 | Foundation C5: dynamic borrow, brands and authority ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c5-dynamic-borrow-brands-and-authority)) | the preservation invariant over owner slots, moves, roots and projections, loans, brands, dependencies and grants is in Lean and proved preserved by each step and across calls; whole-root conflicts, generative brands and grant narrowing are kept; release-context erasure only with its proof ([question 6](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q6)); the old `Borrow`, `Brand` and `Authority` fragments are ported with `open_mut_freezes_root` and `reset_fresh`, and deleted; Home: spec (`Ownership`, `Borrow`, `Brand`, `Authority`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate and the proof-integrity jobs | R-0607, R-0610, R-0612 |
ROADMAP.md:420:| R-0612 | Foundation C6: observations, environment and the concurrency extension ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c6-observations-environment-and-concurrency-extension)) | extensible typed event signatures, request and response matching, finite and infinite traces, terminal observations and the environment relation are in Lean; the trap line, exits 134 and 125, and byte columns with a tab counting one byte ([question 10](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q10)) are rules with examples; the sequential-fragment preservation law for a later concurrency extension is stated; this delivers R-0602's extensible event kind; Home: spec (`Contract`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate (trap-line conformance examples) and the proof-integrity jobs | R-0608 |
ROADMAP.md:421:| R-0613 | Foundation C7: secret leakage and accounting ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c7-secret-leakage-and-accounting)) | the leakage trace, the public-observation relation, release records, the release-policy interface and byte accounting per allocator lineage are in Lean, with the noninterference and constant-time statements as separate theorems over equal release traces; wipe events are observable; Home: spec (`Leakage`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate and the proof-integrity jobs | R-0607 |
ROADMAP.md:422:| R-0614 | Foundation C8: evaluator adequacy and termination ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c8-evaluator-adequacy-and-termination)) | Q9.9's total fuel-indexed evaluator over the hybrid state, with oracle choices checked against operation contracts, is proved sound, complete, monotone in fuel and prefix-consistent against C1's step relation, and adequate for infinite behaviour; `outOfFuel` is only an insufficient budget; Home: spec (`Semantics`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate and the proof-integrity jobs | R-0607 |
ROADMAP.md:423:| R-0615 | Foundation C9: identities, primitive contracts, evidence and ghost erasure ([contract](docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md#c9-identities-primitive-contracts-evidence-and-ghost-erasure)) | the typed identities and rule ids are in Lean (`Ident`, `Rules`, PLAN step 2, on `wip/spec-core`); one primitive-contract interface with a lawful extensible registry refuses unknown operations ([question 16](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q16)); the typed evidence graph and the one versioned diagnostics and facts schema; the struct-invariant exposure definition ([question 15](docs/decisions.md#foundation-q15)); erasure of ownership, brand, loan, accounting and ghost instrumentation is kernel-checked (O3); Home: spec (`Ident`, `Rules`, `Primitives`, `Evidence`, `Facts`). Gate: Spec build, the rule gate, the proof-integrity jobs, and the JSON schema generated from the Lean types with goldens (R-0593) | R-0607, R-0611, R-0613 |
